OL,3,GNEWSA'A man in a balaclava chased me,
OL,4,Abut I won't stop running'
OL,5,
OL,6,FAs the clocks go back and evenings
OL,7,Fbecome darker, many runners face a
OL,8,Fdilemma: stick to the routes they enjoy
OL,9,For change their habits because they do
OL,10,Fnot feel safe.
OL,12,FScarlett Ward refused to let fear make
OL,13,Fthat decision for her, despite a
OL,14,Fterrifying episode when a man in a
OL,15,Fbalaclava chased her down a street.
OL,17,FShe was determined not to give up a
OL,18,Fhobby that had become an important part
OL,19,Fof her life.
OL,23,APub: 05-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
